Made of Standards is released under two licenses, split by what you are reusing.

  Code  — MIT License (below)
  Text  — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)

"Code" means the markup, CSS and JavaScript that make the page work: everything
in index.html that is structure, style or behaviour.

"Text" means the words: the copy rendered on the page, the prose in README.md and
the other documentation in this repository, and the written descriptions the
exhibit displays (timeline entries, specification cluster notes, writing-system
glosses).

Third-party material keeps its own terms: specification names, titles and links
point to W3C publications, and quoted lines remain attributed to their authors.
This project claims no affiliation with W3C.


